<scopecontent><p>Includes judgment for John Norwood vs. Admr. of Elizabeth Brinnon. The suit was a civil suit in which the plaintiff sued for money owed by the defendant for providing Brinnon's servants and enslaved people meat, drink, washing, lodging, and board over a period of twenty years. The suit includes exhibits that record the names of enslaved people, year of birth, year of death, and family relationships.</p></scopecontent>
